parts.text:
Confirmed A2: the bubble view's `onTouchEvent` only handles ACTION_UP and delegates everything else to `super.onTouchEvent(event)`. A plain `View` that is not clickable/long-clickable returns `false` from `super.onTouchEvent`, so the DOWN is not consumed → the view never receives UP → `togglePassthrough()` never runs. The bubble is useless.

Fix: make it clickable and handle DOWN/UP properly.

```kotlin
override fun onTouchEvent(event: MotionEvent): Boolean {
    // View не кликабелен по умолчанию: DOWN уходил в super и терялся,
    // поэтому UP не приходил вовсе, а пузырь ничего не делал.
    when (event.actionMasked) {
        MotionEvent.ACTION_DOWN -> return true
        MotionEvent.ACTION_UP -> { togglePassthrough(); return true }
        MotionEvent.ACTION_CANCEL -> return true
    }
    return super.onTouchEvent(event)
}
```

Also A3: missing FLAG_NOT_TOUCH_MODAL on both windows. Without it, the overlay window covers the whole screen and captures ALL touches (modal behavior), so touches outside the frame/panels get swallowed and never reach the app below. That's a real usability bug. Adding FLAG_NOT_TOUCH_MODAL means touches outside the drawn UI pass through to the app below (within the same window bounds).

Let me check the overlay window params.

