Line 40: `private var readerThemedContext = viewer.activity.createReaderThemeContext()` — a ContextThemeWrapper wrapping the Activity. It's replaced in `refresh()`. Since PagerViewer holds the activity anyway, no extra leak. Fine.

Line 69: `val lastPage = pages.last()` — crash if `currPages` is empty. ChapterLoader guarantees non-empty.

Line 171/176: `items[placeAtIndex]` — `placeAtIndex` could be == items.size (when adding at the end) → `IndexOutOfBoundsException`! Line 180: `items.add(placeAtIndex, newPage)` is valid for placeAtIndex == size. But line 176 `if (items[placeAtIndex] is InsertPage)` would throw IndexOutOfBounds if `placeAtIndex == items.size`. When can that happen? `onPageSplit` is called from PagerPageHolder when dual-page split is enabled and the page is the last one in the chapter. If the current page is the last item in `items` (e.g., last page of the last chapter with no next chapter loaded) then `currentIndex + 1 == items.size` → line 176 → IndexOutOfBoundsException → crash.

Let me check upstream code: In upstream Tachiyomi (1.4.x), `onPageSplit` has:
```
